Registration back-off for a REGISTER that could not be sent, and a refresh
that keeps the registration, issue #77, docs/sip.md.

libre retries a REGISTER that was sent and failed (no answer, an error
response) after 30 to 60 s, doubling to 15 to 30 min (RFC 5626 section
4.5), and starts again from the top on success. One that could not be sent
at all (no network yet, no transport) was not retried by anyone. Now it is
given the same back-off; unregistering still returns the error.

sipreg_refresh sends a REGISTER at once on the same registration: when the
network comes back, a registered account refreshes and one that is backing
off tries now. A new registration (baresip's ua_register) would first
unregister the old one, and the two requests could cross at the server.

